      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Readiness probes misreport Git failures as checkout state",
      "description": "The broad catches treat *any* `gitExec` failure as evidence that the checkout is not a Git checkout or has a detached HEAD. For example, a timeout or permission error from `rev-parse` is reported as `NOT_A_CHECKOUT`, and one from `symbolic-ref` as `DETACHED_HEAD`. In routed fix mode, this turns operational failures into misleading deferral reasons instead of surfacing the underlying problem. Distinguish the expected nonzero exit for these probes from other Git failures.",
